Weakness of sight; loss of perceptive power;
after diphtheria; from exhaustion. Drooping of eye-
lids. [Caust.]

A nervous “gone” sensation at the pit of
the stomach. [Ign.; Sep.; Sulph.] Feels seasick with-
out nausea.

Abdo<men. — Diarrhoea; foul, putrid odor: occasioned
by .fright, with depression and exhaustion. Diarrhoea
while eating. Dysentery; stools consist of pure blood;


